WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:31.360
[Music]

00:00:37.960 --> 00:00:43.720
[Speaker 1:] Oh my god, it's still bleeding. I've had this done a million times before,

00:00:43.733 --> 00:00:51.533
and I've never taken this long for it to stop. I thought you'd never find that vein.

00:00:51.540 --> 00:00:54.633
How many of these things have you given, anyway?

00:00:56.820 --> 00:01:00.133
You're just a student nurse, aren't you?

00:01:01.580 --> 00:01:04.320
I bet you've never given one of these before in your life, have you?

00:01:06.080 --> 00:01:10.033
I don't think that's right.  I don't think you should experiment on me.

00:01:10.040 --> 00:01:12.900
You know, you can get somebody who doesn't count.

00:01:14.400 --> 00:01:17.100
Why don't they get somebody competent to do this kind of thing,

00:01:17.100 --> 00:01:19.380
instead of using us as guinea pigs, you know.

00:01:25.700 --> 00:01:28.633
[Speaker 2:]  Well, I'd really rather talk to the doctor about this.

00:01:28.633 --> 00:01:33.299
I don't want to spend my time talking to you, and then have to repeat it all over.

00:01:33.300 --> 00:01:37.833
I certainly hope I don't have to wait around here for the doctor 30 or 40 minutes.

00:01:38.420 --> 00:01:44.733
I wanted to come in and tell him about this thing, and then get on with it.

00:01:44.733 --> 00:01:48.066
The ladies at the bridge club just drive me crazy.

00:01:48.066 --> 00:01:52.632
They... well... 
I, when I'm the dummy, I have to sit there and wait.

00:01:52.633 --> 00:01:54.533
And I don't want to wait here now.

00:01:54.533 --> 00:02:00.933
I really hope he comes on in.  I want to talk to him about this problem I'm having.

00:02:05.160 --> 00:02:06.940
[Speaker 3:]  Well, how are you today?

00:02:08.060 --> 00:02:12.540
It's real nice to see you again, on an informal basis.

00:02:14.360 --> 00:02:17.180
I have missed our informal chats.

00:02:18.660 --> 00:02:27.240
And I don't quite understand what interfered with our getting together occasionally.

00:02:31.400 --> 00:02:39.580
I do try to share my feelings with you, and others who are working in the program.

00:02:42.160 --> 00:02:43.540
And I do like you.

00:02:45.300 --> 00:02:58.380
But I've had some moments of concern since my position has changed, as to how you are perceiving our working relationship at this point.

00:03:00.340 --> 00:03:15.760
I understand that you have discussed this with others, and I question the advisability of your doing this at this particular time.

00:03:18.060 --> 00:03:25.680
I feel like the both of us have been with the program long enough to understand some things,

00:03:28.000 --> 00:03:36.900
and the necessity for my involvement in scheduling and activities.

00:03:39.040 --> 00:03:49.560
So, although I like you very much, I do question what you do with your time.

00:03:54.333 --> 00:04:09.333
[Speaker 4:]  Hmm-mm... Oh, I'll tell you, I've worried, and I've worried, and now I'm worried.

00:04:09.340 --> 00:04:16.400
It just don't seem like that I can  get ahead on anything.  I'm just...I don't know.

00:04:16.400 --> 00:04:25.060
It just don't seem like that I can make ends meet on the salary that I get.

00:04:25.940 --> 00:04:31.460
And uh, the kids, I've got them on my mind.

00:04:31.466 --> 00:04:36.632
And my wife, it just... it's just something all the time.

00:04:36.633 --> 00:04:44.833
I... it just, it's disgusting and I don't know.

00:04:44.833 --> 00:04:56.866
I, I've tried time and time again to get where I could go and talk to the teacher about the kids.

00:04:56.866 --> 00:05:00.932
She keeps calling, and saying that they're always into something.

00:05:00.940 --> 00:05:04.480
Wanting to know if I'm not going to do anything about it.

00:05:05.500 --> 00:05:08.533
And I don't know.

00:05:08.540 --> 00:05:11.480
And I've got so much on my mind.

00:05:12.140 --> 00:05:17.200
I'm working two jobs, I've got my mind on my wife.

00:05:18.460 --> 00:05:20.833
Now then I've got my kids.

00:05:20.840 --> 00:05:22.600
I just don't know what to do.

00:05:24.400 --> 00:05:31.160
It's beyond me, it... I know that, there is...

00:05:31.166 --> 00:05:38.932
I just might as well give up, because the more I talk about it, the worse I get.

00:05:38.940 --> 00:05:40.280
The worse I feel.

00:05:42.460 --> 00:05:46.533
And I just... it just don't seem that I can get anything over to them.

00:05:46.540 --> 00:05:53.366
Just seem like they... Now my kids, I'm talking about mine,

00:05:53.840 --> 00:06:00.060
seem like they think they know just a little bit than their parents do.

00:06:01.140 --> 00:06:08.700
And I'm just, with my financial situation, and my working status,

00:06:08.700 --> 00:06:11.566
I've just, I've just gone to my limit.

00:06:17.266 --> 00:06:19.466
[Speaker 5:] I used to do all kinds of things.

00:06:36.300 --> 00:06:40.540
I liked learning.

00:06:42.600 --> 00:06:44.033
And uh...

00:06:48.700 --> 00:06:51.300
And I enjoyed things.

00:06:54.640 --> 00:06:57.800
And there was...

00:07:10.860 --> 00:07:13.420
There was a lot I was going to do.

00:07:16.940 --> 00:07:19.760
And now I can't do any of it.

00:07:23.140 --> 00:07:24.920
And I don't understand why.

00:07:37.466 --> 00:07:42.766
[Speaker 6:] I need to talk with you. It's hard for me to say this to you because,

00:07:42.766 --> 00:07:46.199
well, it's hard to put into words the way I feel,

00:07:46.200 --> 00:07:49.966
but I just have to tell you that I've been around here for a long time,

00:07:49.966 --> 00:07:56.566
and you are by far the finest nursing student that I have ever seen on this unit.

00:07:56.566 --> 00:08:01.899
Your competence, your sensitivity, your understanding are just uh, what can I say?

00:08:01.900 --> 00:08:04.066
They're first class.

00:08:04.066 --> 00:08:13.720
I hope that when you graduate from nursing school that you'll seriously consider looking us up, and coming to work for us.

00:08:14.100 --> 00:08:17.400
There's nobody else that I've ever met that has your abilities.

00:08:17.400 --> 00:08:21.760
You're really great, that's all I can say. Will you look us up?

00:08:27.120 --> 00:08:31.600
[Speaker 6:]  I need to talk with you. When people like you come on the ward,

00:08:31.600 --> 00:08:36.633
I make the assumption that they are going to be of some help to us in taking care of our patients.

00:08:36.633 --> 00:08:44.133
Now I've seen people who are students who make minor mistakes, but what you did falls out of the category of a minor mistake,

00:08:44.133 --> 00:08:48.699
and that starts getting into where you can really do some serious damage to another human being.

00:08:48.700 --> 00:08:55.833
Now if you intend to stay on this unit, you will have to make certain that you do not ever make an error like that again.

00:08:55.833 --> 00:09:03.233
That's not just incompetence, that's insensitivity. And the kind of insensitivity that you showed could have killed a patient.

00:09:03.240 --> 00:09:10.120
I don't ever want to see that again on this unit, and I don't ever want to see your face if you ever do anything like that again.

00:09:15.740 --> 00:09:22.260
[Speaker 7:]  Have you been working here since I've been going to the doctor?

00:09:22.260 --> 00:09:26.520
I haven't uh, seen you before.

00:09:29.140 --> 00:09:30.200
Um...

00:09:34.040 --> 00:09:35.220
You're nice!

00:09:38.900 --> 00:09:42.400
It's a good feeling, sweetheart, you ought to try it sometime.

00:09:46.060 --> 00:09:49.500
You really should try it. Mmm.

00:09:56.140 --> 00:10:05.980
Maybe um, maybe after you get off work this evening we could stop by this cute little bar I know.

00:10:07.900 --> 00:10:10.000
Some real cute chicks there.

00:10:15.440 --> 00:10:17.933
[Speaker 8:]  Whew, I'm glad that's over with.

00:10:18.460 --> 00:10:24.333
You know, you're really a really nice person. I've been coming to this place...oh, I've forgotten how long it's been now.

00:10:24.880 --> 00:10:29.733
But I don't know, it seems to me like you and I have a whole lot in common.

00:10:29.733 --> 00:10:32.833
I was wondering, I was thinking about this the other day.

00:10:32.833 --> 00:10:40.433
I don't know what it is, but I really think you and I could really make a go of it other than here 
in this office, you know?

00:10:40.433 --> 00:10:46.833
So why don't you give me your phone number, and maybe we can set up a date sometime, and go out and,

00:10:46.833 --> 00:10:55.166
I don't know, do whatever you want to do, and I think I've got a few friends that you might be interested in, too.

00:10:55.166 --> 00:10:58.460
I've got several friends. They drop into my apartment all the time.

00:10:59.800 --> 00:11:05.360
And I don't know, I think you and I could really hit it off because I've already noticed that we have a lot in common.

00:11:09.940 --> 00:11:12.000
[Speaker 9:] I'm glad you stopped by.

00:11:15.700 --> 00:11:22.540
You know, I've been here for a while now, and I've had a lot of time to think about things.

00:11:25.860 --> 00:11:33.220
Well, I've been thinking a lot about you, especially in the last three or four nights.

00:11:35.860 --> 00:11:39.600
You've been telling me what a great patient I've been, but...

00:11:41.440 --> 00:11:44.920
I don't know if I've ever told you what a fantastic person you are.

00:11:51.300 --> 00:11:55.400
I think what I'm trying to say is that I really like you a lot.

00:11:57.040 --> 00:12:02.860
And you know I'd like to be friends with you. I mean close friends.

00:12:03.760 --> 00:12:08.920
Yeah, I'd maybe even like to get together with you when you have some time.

00:12:09.480 --> 00:12:12.420
We could see each other when I got out of the hospital.

00:12:14.040 --> 00:12:16.260
I think we have a lot in common.

00:12:19.760 --> 00:12:21.420
How do you feel about that?

00:12:26.766 --> 00:12:30.666
[Speaker 10:] You know, you have problems, I understand that. Everyone has problems.

00:12:30.666 --> 00:12:34.099
But you have made an occupation out of having problems.

00:12:34.100 --> 00:12:37.766
We are not running a therapy institute here.

00:12:37.766 --> 00:12:43.799
I cannot afford to deal with you and your personal problems constantly on an hour-by-hour basis,

00:12:43.800 --> 00:12:45.933
nor can the people that you work with.

00:12:45.933 --> 00:12:47.866
You're not a child anymore.

00:12:47.866 --> 00:12:51.466
This is not the type of organization that we have here.

00:12:51.466 --> 00:12:57.966
Somewhere down the line, you're going to have to make a commitment to being able to work out things yourself on your own.

00:12:57.966 --> 00:13:03.132
We cannot afford to deal with this type of material day after day, week after week.

00:13:03.133 --> 00:13:06.666
Do you have any idea how other people relate to you here?

00:13:06.666 --> 00:13:10.360
Do you have any idea how you're coming across to everyone?

00:13:25.440 --> 00:13:32.180
[Speaker 11:]  Hey, Florence Nightingale. Come here.

